From f2f5c45791bdc91461f09a24085c626a82df74d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:52:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] expert_pack tier: O(log n) heap victim selection and FIFO
 transient pool

Retained victims come from a lazy min-heap keyed (access_count, last_access,
slot_index), identical to the previous full scan including tie-break.
Transient entries use transient_slots (default 4*top_k) extra VRAM slots
allocated on top of cache_vram_mib and reused FIFO, so a slot just read by
layer k's kernel is not overwritten by layer k+1's H2D.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
